{"display":"I want to solve the problem of treating tickets as isolated implementation tasks.\n\nI want to better understand the user problem, product impact, and operational risks behind each ticket, so that I can feel more ownership, ask better questions, and become more immersed in my work.","pastedContents":{},"timestamp":1779584715728,"project":"/Users/mingyumkim/Study/deliberate-practice","sessionId":"1652522a-77fa-44c3-b393-abe78f3f7089"}
{"display":"[Pasted text #1 +16 lines]","pastedContents":{"1":{"id":1,"type":"text","content":"In order to create a sense of immersion, this training needs to be directly connected to the work I am actually responsible for.\n\nFor example:\n\n- Draw the overall flow and explain to myself what role my part plays in that flow.\n- Write down how this work may affect users.\n  - What user problem can be solved through this work?\n  - Are there alternative ways to approach the problem besides the current solution? What are the pros and cons?\n  - What operational gaps or user failure scenarios could this work create? Can they be prevented or detected in advance?\n- Think about whether I can test this from the user’s perspective in advance, and how I can verify the impact on users after deployment.\n  - API\n  - DB\n  - logs\n  - dashboards\n  - metrics\n  - test automation\n- Check whether I shared the organized questions or findings with a senior developer or manager."}},"timestamp":1779584755342,"project":"/Users/mingyumkim/Study/deliberate-practice","sessionId":"1652522a-77fa-44c3-b393-abe78f3f7089"}
